  <running_head>INSTITUTIONUM</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">continentibus tantum reperiuntur.</l>
    <l n="2">Adjungantur vero ultimo argumento</l>
    <l n="3">præcedentia, sic urgentius stringet.</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">V. <i>Divisa vero illa materia est in</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>diversas partes, quas tum in similares &amp;</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>dissimilares: tum in communes &amp; proprias</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>non male dividere licet.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8" para="true">§. De communibus &amp; propriis par-</l>
    <l n="9">tibus hoc ita intellige: quod quædam</l>
    <l n="10">partes sentientes quidem sunt, sed non</l>
    <l n="11">primario illis specialis sensus exercetur,</l>
    <l n="12">verum communis tantum sentiendi</l>
    <l n="13">potestas, atque illas ideo communes</l>
    <l n="14">dicimus: aliæ vero partes sensui parti-</l>
    <l n="15">culariter &amp; perfecte exercendo dicatæ</l>
    <l n="16">sunt, quas ideo proprias appellamus.</l>
    <l n="17">Attamen licet &amp; alio sensu communes</l>
    <l n="18">partes vocare, quæ animalibus omni-</l>
    <l n="19">bus competunt: proprias vero, quæ</l>
    <l n="20">quibusdam tantum: ut supra plantarum</l>
    <l n="21">partes ea ratione digessimus.</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">VI. <i>Partes animalium communes</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>sunt vel liquidæ vel consistentes.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24" para="true">§. Hippocrat. l. 6. Epid. partes o-</l>
    <l n="25">mnes dividit in ἰχῶρας, ἰχώδεα</l>
    <l n="26">καὶ ὀρμώδεα. i. e. continentia, contenta, &amp;</l>
    <l n="27">impetum facientia. Nos vero ἰχώδεα</l>
    <l n="28">καὶ ὀρμώδεα sub liquidis comprehendi-</l>
    <l n="29">mus, &amp; ἰχῶρας solidarum partium no-</l>
    <l n="30">mine insignimus, secuti hac in parte</l>
    <l n="31">Arist.</l>
  </main_text>
